@* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Components/App.razor — the root component (checklist task 67).

   This is the ONE document shell of the application: it carries everything the four master pages
   each declared in their own <!DOCTYPE>/<html>/<head>/<body> — the meta tags, the stylesheet and
   script references the WebForms theme engine used to auto-inject, and the inline <style> blocks
   of MixERPMaster/BackendMaster. Layouts (Components/Layout/*.razor) are fragments and must not
   repeat any of it; a layout that needs extra head content uses <HeadContent>.

   MUST NOT BE REMOVED (Specialist 3's note):
     * <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" /> — every migrated control that sets a page
       title or head content (ReportEngine, ScrudFactory, ReportLayout, BlankLayout, ...) renders
       through it.
     * <link href="MixERP.Net.FrontEnd.styles.css" /> — the host scoped-CSS bundle carrying every
       referenced RCL's .razor.css.
     * <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
     * The global @rendermode="InteractiveServer" on <Routes> and <HeadOutlet>. It is declared
       HERE and ONLY here: a page that also declares @rendermode would be a nested render-mode
       error.

   data-ng-app="MixERPApp" is kept from BackendMaster (the angular module the backend pages
   bootstrap). lang="en" is kept from MixERPMaster.

   The IE 8/9 shims (html5shiv, respond.js) and the IE-only ".grid3 td" conditional comment were
   dropped: conditional comments are not honoured by any browser that can run Blazor.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *@
@using System.Globalization

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-ng-app="MixERPApp">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no" />
    <meta name="description" content="MixERP" />
    <base href="/" />
    <title>MixERP: ASP.net ERP</title>

    @* The former master-page bundles. master-page.min.css bundles colorbox, jquery-ui,
       jstree, semantic-ui and the mixerp theme; the explicit mixerp.min.css link is the theme
       stylesheet App_Themes used to inject automatically (flagged by Specialist 1). *@
    <link href="/bundles/stylesheets/master-page.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <link href="/css/themes/mixerp/mixerp.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Titillium+Web" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="MixERP.Net.FrontEnd.styles.css" />

    @* Inline <style> of MixERPMaster.Master / BackendMaster.Master, preserved verbatim. *@
    <style>
        #right {
            padding: 0;
            margin: 0;
        }

        .widget {
            cursor: move;
        }

        .widget i {
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>

    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>
<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />

    @* /Resources.js is the localized client resource script (MixERP.Net.i18n ResourcesEndpoint,
       mapped by Program.cs). BackendMaster requested it with the current two-letter language, so
       the same query value is emitted here — App.razor is statically rendered per request, so
       CultureInfo.CurrentCulture is the request's (and therefore the user's) culture. *@
    <script src="/Resources.js?culture=@CultureInfo.CurrentCulture.TwoLetterISOLanguageName"></script>

    @* The master-page script bundle (jquery, angular, jquery-ui, semantic-ui, signalr, jstree,
       mixerp-core and the master-page scripts, including the rewritten notification.js). All four
       master pages loaded a subset of this bundle; the blank and report masters loaded only
       libraries.min.js, a strict subset, so loading the full bundle for every page adds scripts
       but removes none. *@
    <script src="/bundles/scripts/master-page.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/mixerp/master-page/layout-interop.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/mixerp/master-page/eod.js"></script>

    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
